---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

/**
 * The page Twilio / TCR reviewers open during toll-free verification.
 *
 * Rejection code 30513 wants documented opt-in; the consent checkbox on
 * /contact plus the opt-in section below is that documentation. Code 30445
 * wants the business verifiable — the name, service area, business phone and
 * business-domain email all appear here and in the footer, and must match the
 * Twilio registration exactly.
 *
 * ⚠️ Have this reviewed before publishing.
 */
const updated = 'July 31, 2026';
---

<Legal
  title="SMS Terms | Rocky Mountain Booking"
  description="Text messaging terms for Rocky Mountain Booking: appointment confirmations and review requests, message frequency, rates, and how to opt out with STOP or get help with HELP."
  path="/sms-terms"
  heading="SMS Terms"
  updated={updated}
  intro={`These terms cover the text messages sent by ${site.legalName}. That includes the messages our system sends on behalf of a client business, and the messages we send to our own clients.`}
>
  <h2>Program name</h2>
  <p>
    The program is <strong>Rocky Mountain Booking</strong>. Messages are sent by{' '}
    {site.legalName}, {site.city}, {site.state}.
  </p>

  <h2>The two kinds of message we send</h2>

  <h3>1. Appointment confirmations and reminders</h3>
  <p>
    When someone books an appointment through a business that uses our service, we text them a
    confirmation with the business name, the date and time, and the address. We may also send a
    reminder before the appointment, and a message if the appointment is changed or cancelled.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Review requests (Review Bot)</h3>
  <p>
    A few hours after an appointment is completed, we send one message asking the customer to leave
    a review, with a link. Every customer receives the same message regardless of how the job went.
    We do not screen customers before asking, we do not route unhappy customers somewhere else, and
    we do not offer anything in exchange for a review.
  </p>

  <p>
    We also send our own client businesses operational notifications. New bookings, urgent call
    alerts, and periodic summaries of calls handled.
  </p>

  <p>
    All of these are transactional or service messages.{' '}
    <strong>We do not send marketing or promotional text messages.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>How you opt in</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Callers and customers.</strong> You opt in verbally during a call you placed to a
    business that uses our service. Our assistant asks whether it may text a confirmation to the
    number you are calling from, and your answer is recorded and timestamped. If you decline, we do
    not text you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Business enquiries.</strong> If you contact us through the form on this website, there
    is an optional checkbox to receive text messages about your enquiry. It is unchecked by default,
    it is never required in order to submit the form, and we record both the timestamp and the exact
    wording shown to you at the time.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Client businesses.</strong> You opt in by providing your mobile number and agreeing to
    notifications when your service is set up.
  </p>
  <p>We never text someone to ask for consent, and we do not buy, rent, or import phone lists.</p>

  <h2>Message frequency</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Message frequency varies</strong> and depends on activity. A customer booking an
    appointment typically receives one to three messages per appointment. Client businesses receive
    messages as calls come in, plus periodic summaries.
  </p>

  <h2>Cost</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Message and data rates may apply.</strong> We do not charge you for text messages. Any
    charges come from your own mobile carrier under your own plan.
  </p>

  <h2>How to stop messages</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Reply STOP to any message.</strong> You will get one confirmation that you have been
    unsubscribed, and then nothing further to that number. You can also contact us at{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or{' '}
    <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a> to be removed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Opting out of messages does not cancel a booked appointment. To change or cancel an appointment,
    call the business directly.
  </p>

  <h2>How to get help</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Reply HELP to any message</strong>, or contact us at{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or{' '}
    <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Carriers</h2>
  <p>
    Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. Delivery depends on your
    carrier&rsquo;s network and is not guaranteed.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Mobile opt-in data and consent are never shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing
      purposes.
    </strong>{' '}
    Full detail is in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
